 r←DropBody block;CR;LF;a;b
⍝ `block` is raw HTTP data as received. Returns its header part: everything up to and including
⍝ the empty line that ends the header. When there is no such line, `block` is returned when its
⍝ first line is a request line (the header was not complete yet), and '' otherwise: then `block`
⍝ is part of a body, or the rest of a header whose start is gone, and cannot be told apart.
 (CR LF)←⎕UCS 13 10
 a←((CR,LF,CR,LF)⍷block)⍳1
 b←((LF,LF)⍷block)⍳1
 :If a<b
     r←(a+3)↑block
 :ElseIf b≤≢block
     r←(b+1)↑block
 :ElseIf ∨/' HTTP/'⍷block↑⍨¯1+⌊/block⍳CR LF
     r←block
 :Else
     r←''
 :EndIf
